  "description": "\u201cThe intersection of the three interior angle bisectors and center of the inscribed circle of triangle ABC.\u201d\n\u2014 Clark Kimberling's Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers (ETC) \u2022 X_1 (Incenter)\n\nInteractive GEOMETOR Explorer page: https://geometor.github.io/etc/centers/c-00001-00019/x-00001/\n\n1 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: X_1 = Incenter \u2022 [A I_a] \u2229 [B I_b] \u2229 [C I_c]\n2 \u00b7 GOAL: X_1 = Incenter \u2022 [A I_a] \u2229 [B I_b] \u2229 [C I_c]\n3 \u00b7 ASSERT: Trilinears 1 : 1 : 1 \u2022 Barycentrics a : b : c\n4 \u00b7 INTERSECT: Nagel Line {1, 2, 8, 10} \u2022 Feuerbach Line {1, 5, 11}\n5 \u00b7 INTERSECT: Nagel Line {1, 2, 8, 10} \u2022 Feuerbach Line {1, 5, 11}\n6 \u00b7 PROVE: Self-Isogonal (X_1) \u2022 Complement X_10 \u2022 Anticomplement X_8\n7 \u00b7 \u2234: Kimberling (6, 9, 13) Search = 1.690308509457\n\nGEOMETOR \u2022 ETC \u2022 X_1",
